[DHL API Developer Portal]

Dear valued customer,


DHL is modernizing its global API platform to ensure long=E2=80=91term reli=
ability, security, and scalability. Our goal is to complete this transition=
 **without impacting your service**, but depending on your system setup, ce=
rtain adjustments or checks may be required.

#### Potential Impacts & Recommended Actions
--------------------------------------------

#### 1. Header Names Will Be Lower=E2=80=91Case Going Forward
-----------------------------------------------------

After the modernization, all HTTP header names will be delivered back in **=
lower=E2=80=91case**, as required by HTTP/2. Previously, some headers may h=
ave appeared in **Camel=E2=80=91Case**=C2=A0or **UPPERCASE** formats. **Hea=
der values remain unchanged.**
Even when communication falls back to HTTP/1.1, header names will still app=
ear in lower=E2=80=91case.

Recommended actions:

- Ensure your system treats header names as case=E2=80=91insensitive, as de=
fined by the HTTP specification.
- If your applications rely on case=E2=80=91sensitive header processing, pl=
ease update them accordingly.

#### 2. Updated Network IP Addresses
------------------------------------

The modernized platform uses a new set of IP addresses.
Most customers using domain=E2=80=91based communication will not need to ta=
ke action.
Customers with strict firewall rules or IP allow=E2=80=91lists may be affec=
ted.
=C2=A0
**Recommended actions:**

- If you rely only on domain names, no changes are needed.
- If your systems use IP allow=E2=80=91lists, please update them using the =
following addresses:

[Image]

#### 3. Updated Cipher Requirements for Encrypted Connections
-------------------------------------------------------------

The modernized platform supports only secure, up=E2=80=91to=E2=80=91date ci=
phers.
Older or insecure cipher configurations will no longer be accepted.
=C2=A0
**Recommended actions:**

- Ensure your systems use any of the following ciphers:
    - TLS 1.3
        - TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256
        - TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384
    - TLS 1.2
        - TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256
        - TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384

#### Testing
------------

To ensure a smooth transition, we recommend:

- Testing your integrations in the sandbox environment.
    - Sandbox testing is supported using the production API key for a limit=
ed time during migration.
    - Sandbox endpoint: [https://t.dhl.com/go/11/FW8I-6UNY0M2V-6UNYCAIM-FO2=
FOZ.html](https://api-sandbox.dhl.com/location-finder/)
- Validating authentication, connectivity, and compatibility with your syst=
ems

#### Support
------------

If you need assistance or have questions:

- Contact your DHL representative, or
- Submit a ticket via the Developer Portal Help Center: [https://t.dhl.com/=
go/11/FW8I-6UNY0M2V-6UNYCAIN-11EQVIJ.html](https://support-developer.dhl.co=
m/support/tickets/new)

#### Timeline
-------------

The Location Finder API changes will be introduced as part of the upcoming =
platform modernization.

- HTTP header name changes (conversion to lower case) are scheduled to take=
 effect on 28 May.
- Network IP address changes are planned for the period 22=E2=80=9329 June.
- Cipher suite updates are planned for the period 22=E2=80=9329 June.=20
A grace period applies, and customers should ensure that their systems supp=
ort the required cipher suites.

#### Next Steps
---------------

- Review the three potential impact areas
- Test your integrations in the sandbox
- Prepare any required updates with your internal teams
- Reach out early if you require clarification

Thank you for your cooperation and continued partnership.=E2=80=8C
**Your DHL API Developer Portal Team**
DHL Group
